  "id": "COMPOUND:25088 - PROTEIN:3691",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Galbanic Acid and Arginine deiminase through a series of target interactions involving Cis-Bis(Methylthio)Silvatin and Ligustrone A. Galbanic Acid is linked to ATP-binding cassette sub-family A member 1 and Cholesteryl ester transfer protein, both of which are targets of Cis-Bis(Methylthio)Silvatin, which in turn targets Arginine deiminase. Similarly, Galbanic Acid is also linked to HCT-8, which is a target of Ligustrone A, which also targets Arginine deiminase. These findings indicate that Galbanic Acid may influence the activity of Arginine deiminase through different pathways, possibly via the activation of Cis-Bis(Methylthio)Silvatin or Ligustrone A. The scores from the paths suggest a consistent level of confidence in the relationship, but the exact mechanism by which Galbanic Acid modulates Arginine deiminase remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a complex network of interactions, highlighting the importance of further investigation into the molecular pathways involved.",
